//  - Raid, with Beacon of Virtue: Divine Toll (and Aura Mastery, with Ringing of the Heavens) inside the Beacon window.
//  - Avenging Wrath: the normal rotation, just more healing (30 s with Sanctified Wrath; Call of the Righteous: 90 s).
//  - Never a generator at 5 Holy Power (Divine Toll on 1 or 2 is fine, so a little is expected).
// And WoWAnalyzer's Holy Paladin module for Midnight 12.0 (github.com/WoWAnalyzer/WoWAnalyzer, the midnight branch): only
// Flash of Light and Judgment spend Infusion of Light; never hard cast Flash of Light (without a proc); a cooldown graph with
// the time a whole extra use fit marked red.
// Talents are read from what the log shows: Dawnlight (Herald of the Sun), Holy Bulwark (Lightsmith), Beacon of Virtue or
// Beacon of Faith, Avenging Crusader, Holy Shock pressed twice within its cooldown (2 charges), Infusion of Light at 2 stacks.
// And for Judgment, Holy Power and mana (Wowhead's rotation guide and its Common Mistakes and Mana Management tabs, Icy Veins' rotation
// page, WoWAnalyzer's Judgment, Crusader's Might, Empyrean Legacy and Infusion of Light modules, and each talent's tooltip on Wowhead):
//  - Judgment is a filler, near the bottom of the healing priority: 1 Holy Power (2 with an Infusion of Light, which also makes Greater
//    Judgment stronger). "Casting Judgment too much" is a common mistake: an Infusion belongs on Flash of Light whenever anyone needs
//    healing. WoWAnalyzer gives it no cast efficiency on purpose. Holy Shock comes before it.
//  - Its talents: Greater Judgment (the target deals less damage), Truth Prevails (it heals you, 30% less mana), Divine Revelations (an
//    Infused one refunds 0.5% mana), Divine Glimpse (+8% crit), Crusader's Might (Holy Shock and Crusader Strike take 1.5 s off it, wasted
//    when it's already ready), Empyrean Legacy (a Judgment crit makes the next Word of Glory or Eternal Flame also cast Light of Dawn, at
//    most once every 20 s), Awakening (a spender can make the next Judgment crit; Avenging Wrath grants it), Hammer of Wrath (Judgment
//    becomes it during Avenging Wrath), Veneration, Righteous Judgment. The tier set's 4 pieces: Judgment has a 20% chance to grant an
//    Infusion, and every Holy Light grants one (only with the set: seen in the log, never assumed).
//  - Holy Power: Holy Shock, Judgment, Flash of Light and Holy Light all build it (the log names Flash of Light's and Holy Light's
//    "Beacon of Light"); never build at 5. Eternal Flame is the best spender, Light of Dawn only when Eternal Flame would overheal a lot.
//  - Mana: Holy Light is how you spend it (more when there's mana to spare, fewer when running low); end near empty without running out.
// Infusion of Light carries 2 uses per proc with Inflorescence of the Sunwell, 1 without (the talent when the log has it; otherwise the
// log's own stacks).
